{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOperator ruling (recorded on this ticket and executed for the CLI/library surface in\n39f8-ae7c, merged as Gerrit change 2045 / commit 91e5ef893d): **\"Unreadable config should\nresult in an error.\"** `gate_enabled` now raises `ConfigError` on an unreadable\n`rebar.toml`, and the CLI (`main()` boundary) and library (`rebar.claim`/`rebar.transition`\ndocstrings + the `rebar.ConfigError` re-export) surface it. Two sibling resolvers in\n`src/rebar/config.py` still collapse the same config-read FAULT into the configured/default\nvalue, and the MCP adapter cannot surface the fault at all (change 2045's PS4 surface-parity\nadvisory, `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py`):\n\n* `config.mcp_readonly()` — `except ConfigError: return True`. A broken config reads as the\n  `mcp.readonly` POLICY choice. Consumed by `mcp_server._readonly` (write-tool registration)\n  and `runner_support._readonly_gate` (comment-tool withholding).\n* `config.mcp_gate(attr, *, fail)` — `except ConfigError: return fail`. Same collapse for\n  `mcp.allow_llm` / `mcp.allow_jira_sync`, consumed by `mcp_server._mcp_gate` via\n  `_allow_llm` / `_allow_jira_sync` (per-request checks in `_mcp_llm.py` tools and\n  `_mcp_writes.py` workflow LLM-step gating).\n\nPer the ruling this is no longer \"distinguish the states, keep the safe fail direction\"\n(the pre-ruling approach below is superseded): a config fault must ERROR loudly, never\nsilently resolve to a default — even a safe one — because a fault that reads as a policy\nchoice never gets fixed.\n\n## Approach\n\nRaise at the SOURCE, mirroring the 39f8-ae7c seam exactly (one posture, one message shape):\n\n1. `config.mcp_readonly()` drops its `except ConfigError: return True`; it re-raises a\n   `ConfigError` chained `from` the parse fault, naming the gate (\"the MCP read-only gate\")\n   and citing operator ruling 39f8-ae7c, in the same message shape `gates.gate_enabled` uses.\n2. `config.mcp_gate(attr)` does the same (naming \"the mcp.<attr> gate\"). Its `fail`\n   keyword existed ONLY to pick the malformed-config fallback, so it is now dead and is\n   REMOVED; `mcp_server._mcp_gate` drops the parameter it merely forwarded, and\n   `_allow_llm` / `_allow_jira_sync` update their calls and their \"Fail-SAFE off\" comments\n   to the new error posture. (No third tri-state is minted anywhere — the pre-ruling idea\n   of reusing `GateState` is dead: `GateState` is back to a two-value policy enum and the\n   fault path is an exception, exactly as in 39f8.)\n3. MCP surfacing (the 2045 PS4 surface-parity advisory): `_mcp_errors._envelope_error`\n   adds `ConfigError` to its known-exception set, and `_errors.error_code_for` classifies\n   `ConfigError` to a NEW vocabulary code `config_unreadable` (added to\n   `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`), so an MCP tool hitting an unreadable config returns the structured\n   envelope (machine-readable code + the parse-fault message) instead of an opaque crash.\n   The addition is additive and covered by the held-out envelope contract tests\n   (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_mcp_error_envelope_*.py`), which pin\n   code∈`KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`.\n4. `runner_support._readonly_gate` needs no code change — the error now propagates out of\n   the shared resolver — but its \"fails CLOSED (read-only)\" docstring paragraph is\n   retargeted to the error posture.\n5. Server startup already fails closed on an unreadable config (`build_server` reads\n   composed config via `compose_config`, which propagates `ConfigError`); registration-time\n   `ctx.readonly()` propagation is consistent with that documented contract.\n6. Docs: `docs/config.md` (the mcp gate bullets' fail-direction sentences),\n   `docs/mcp-reference.md` (error-envelope vocabulary gains `config_unreadable`), and —\n   the second 2045 PS4 advisory, same ruling — `docs/event-schema.md`'s stale\n   `gate_unreadable` text (still described as \"unreadable config, gate failed open\") is\n   retargeted to: historical value only, no new write produces it, an unreadable config\n   errors per 39f8-ae7c.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — `mcp_readonly` / `mcp_gate` raise; `fail` kwarg removed.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — `_mcp_gate`, `_allow_llm`, `_allow_jira_sync` signature/\n  comment updates.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py` — `ConfigError` in the envelope guard's known set.\n- `src/rebar/_errors.py` — `config_unreadable` in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` + `error_code_for`\n  branch (before the generic `error_code` attribute step; ConfigError carries none).\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py` — `_readonly_gate` docstring retarget.\n- `docs/config.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, `docs/event-schema.md` — contract text.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — entry under [Unreleased] (behavior change on the MCP surface).\n- Tests: retarget `tests/unit/test_config_ev3a_aliases.py`\n  (`test_mcp_readonly_fails_closed_on_malformed` → raises; the `allow_llm` garbage-env arm\n  → raises); new RED module `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py`;\n  envelope-code coverage rides the existing held-out contract suites.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED before GREEN (the new module fails on current main, passes after):\n\n- Happy/failure pairs at each resolver: readable config on/off → the configured bool for\n  `mcp_readonly()` and `mcp_gate(\"allow_llm\")`; malformed `rebar.toml`/`pyproject.toml` →\n  `ConfigError` raised, chained from the parse fault, message naming the gate and the\n  ruling.\n- Consumer propagation: `mcp_server._readonly` / `_allow_llm` and\n  `runner_support._readonly_gate` propagate the typed error (no swallow anywhere on the\n  path).\n- MCP envelope: `_envelope_error(ConfigError(...))` returns an `McpEnvelopeError` whose\n  envelope carries `error == \"config_unreadable\"`; `rebar.error_code_for(ConfigError(...))\n  == \"config_unreadable\"` and the code is in `rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`.\n- Invariance guards: readable-config resolution byte-identical (file key honored, env\n  wins), existing ev3a alias tests stay green minus the two retargeted arms.\n- Full gates: `make lint`, targeted pytest for the modules above plus the held-out\n  envelope contract suites, `make typecheck`, complexity ratchet.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] With a malformed config, `config.mcp_readonly()` and `config.mcp_gate(attr)` raise\n  `ConfigError` (chained from the parse fault, message naming the gate and ruling\n  39f8-ae7c) instead of returning a bool — checked by the new\n  `test_mcp_gate_unreadable_config_errors_8408.py`.\n- [x] The `fail` kwarg is gone from `config.mcp_gate` and `mcp_server._mcp_gate`; no\n  caller passes a malformed-config fallback anywhere — checked by grep in review and the\n  updated call sites compiling under mypy.\n- [x] An MCP tool failing on an unreadable config yields the structured envelope with the\n  new `config_unreadable` code — checked by the new module (envelope unit arm) and the\n  held-out contract suites staying green with the enlarged vocabulary.\n- [x] `runner_support._readonly_gate` propagates the error (no catch on the path) —\n  checked by the new module's consumer-propagation arm.\n- [x] A readable config's behaviour is byte-identical (file key honored, env wins, both\n  policy values resolve as before) — checked by the surviving ev3a alias tests.\n- [x] `docs/config.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`, and `docs/event-schema.md` state the new\n  contract (unreadable config ⇒ error; `gate_unreadable` historical-only) — checked by\n  reading the three updated sections.\n- [x] Exactly one fault posture exists: no new tri-state enum, no second copy of\n  `GateState` — checked in review.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787379979605824001,"uuid":"d9ef9cd9-f256-4540-af90-2a2ec20cb2a6"}